Local modifications (each lands as its own commit on top of the drop):

8. Inline codegen + default-on. The hot-loop path now runs in native
   registers/memory with NO per-op call: constants, get/put/set_loc,
   get_loc0_loc1, int arithmetic/bitwise/comparison (both-int inline,
   overflow/non-int -> slow), inc/dec/inc_loc/dec_loc, if_true/false
   truthiness, and the backedge interrupt (inline counter decrement).
   Refcount inc is inlined; free/put on heap values fall to helpers via
   a tag check. Prologue caches stack_buf/var_buf/arg_buf/ctx in saved
   regs (6 scratch, 6 saved). RESULT: 3.4-4.7x faster than the
   interpreter on hot numeric loops (was ~1.13x call-threaded).
   ybrowser-js.c: JIT is now DEFAULT ON (baseline); YBROWSER_JS_JIT=off
   disables, =eager compiles all. SLJIT flag gotcha fixed: SUB sets a
   flag with the CANONICAL condition (SIG_LESS/SIG_GREATER/Z); the
   inverse (…_EQUAL) is read via op_flags, not SET. NOTE: valgrind
   cannot trace SLJIT's dual-mapped W^X memory (false crash) — ASan is
   the authoritative check and is clean (differential + stress).

7. Stage 6 platform gating. quickjs.cmake compiles the JIT in ONLY on
   Linux x86-64 (validated); every other platform builds interpreter-
   only with the JS_JIT* API stubs (JS_JITAvailable()==0), verified by a
   no-JIT build of the engine + selftest. Per-platform enablement
   checklist documented in quickjs.cmake. QJS_ENABLE_JIT=OFF disables
   entirely.

6. Stage 5 JIT hardening. W^X: SLJIT PROT dual-mapping allocator
   (SLJIT_PROT_EXECUTABLE_ALLOCATOR=1 in quickjs.cmake) — code never
   RWX. Thread-wide native-code cap (qjs_jit_thread_code_bytes, 64MB)
   alongside the per-runtime cap; both checked before compile, released
   on free. Tests: test/ybrowser/jit/jit-stress.c (differential +
   create/eval/destroy cycles) and the interruptibility check in
   jit-selftest.c; run.sh drives plain + ASan/UBSan builds under a
   timeout. Verified: ASan/UBSan clean, differential clean, WPT 115/115
   eager AND baseline, JIT infinite loop interrupted via backedge
   safe-points.

5. Stage 4 JIT object operations. quickjs-jit-compile.c: property /
   element access (get_field/get_field2/get_length/put_field/
   get_array_el/get_array_el2/put_array_el via JS_GetPropertyInternal /
   JS_SetPropertyInternal2 / JS_GetPropertyValue / JS_SetPropertyValue,
   consumed slots nulled), closure vars (get/put/set_var_ref +short
   +_check), and call/constructor expansion (call_method,
   call_constructor, tail_call/tail_call_method returning the result).
   Atom/index operands re-read from bytecode at pc_off. Return lowering
   frees operands below the result. Verified: prop/array/method/closure/
   constructor cases + throws, valgrind-clean (ownership), WPT 115/115
   eager. Stage 4b guarded inline-cache load remains a perf refinement
   (Stage 0 audit found no reusable 0.15.0 IC records; JS_GetProperty*
   already does the internal shape lookup).

4. Stage 3 JIT arithmetic. quickjs-jit-compile.c: binary
   arith/logic/compare (both-int fast path inline, exact interpreter
   slow fn otherwise — js_add_slow/js_binary_arith_slow/js_shr_slow/
   js_relational_slow/js_eq_slow/js_strict_eq_slow/js_binary_logic_slow),
   unary (neg/plus/not/lnot/inc/dec), post_inc/dec, inc_loc/dec_loc,
   add_loc (string+slow, consumed slot nulled for unwind), get_loc0_loc1.
   op/pc packed into helper arg words (function len < 1MB). Verified:
   real loops (sum/mul/nested/fib/while), valgrind-clean, WPT 115/115
   eager; ~1.13x on a pure-int loop (call-threaded; inline int codegen
   is a later perf refinement).

3. Stage 2 JIT control flow. quickjs-jit-compile.c: worklist stack-depth
   pre-pass, per-target SLJIT labels + jump patching, exception-unwind
   path (free live operands, return -1) matching the interpreter's
   `exception:`; lowerings for stack manip, locals/args (incl. TDZ
   get/put_loc_check), branches (if_true/false + goto, backward-edge
   interrupt safe-point), and the call family. ybrowser-js.c:
   YBROWSER_JS_JIT env toggle. Status helpers return sljit_sw (a 32-bit
   int return leaves the upper reg bits undefined → misread -1).
   Verified: jit-selftest.c (interp/eager/baseline agree incl. exception
   unwind), valgrind-clean, WPT 115/115 with eager JIT on real page JS.

2. Stage 1 baseline JIT skeleton (SLJIT backend). NEW files:
   quickjs-jit-compile.c (bytecode->SLJIT translator; #included via
   quickjs-jit.c under QJS_ENABLE_JIT); sljit/ vendored (own UPSTREAM).
   quickjs.c: JSFunctionBytecode jitc_* fields, JSRuntime jit field,
   JS_CallInternal tiering+dispatch hook (reuses the interpreter frame),
   free_function_bytecode + JS_NewRuntime2 hooks — all under
   QJS_ENABLE_JIT. Public control API (JS_JITSetMode/Available/GetStats)
   in quickjs-jit.h. Compiles constants + return; mixed-tier verified
   against the interpreter (test/ybrowser/jit/jit-selftest.c).

